Cell["\<\
Arranged in increasing generality: 
0) a1[t_] is used to test scalar derivatives. 
1) a1[] is most restricted test vector where variables of coordinate system \
is used as coefficients at corresponding basis elements of PointVector[ ]. In \
fact it represents Point vector. 
2) aa1[ h_] is more general test vector, where in the PointVector the \
coordinate is replaced by the same function h of that coordinate
3) aa1[ ] is further generalization of test vector, where in the PointVector \
the coordinate is replaced by the different functions of single variable of \
that coordinate system 
4) aaa1[ h_] is further generalization of test vector, where in the \
PointVector the coordinate is replaced by  same function h of all variables \
of that coordinate system
5) aaa1[] is most general vector function, where in the PointVector the \
coordinate is replaced by the different functions of all variables of \
coordinate system\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.673770213170585*^9, 3.673770271212688*^9}, {
   3.673770498050648*^9, 3.673770512428942*^9}, {3.67377085466058*^9, 
   3.673770874134313*^9}, {3.673847424440953*^9, 3.673847454297884*^9}, {
   3.67384748908961*^9, 3.673847491281632*^9}, {3.67385142912274*^9, 
