Cell["\<\
Short explanation. First, we define the manifold we will work on. This is \
realised with  gaDefinePositionVector[ ]. After manifold is defined we define \
coordinate system (frame) on that manifold . The coordinate system has to \
have its own name, since we can define different coordinate or non-coordinate \
systems on the same manifold. Coordinate system is defined with  \
gaDefineCoordinateChart[]name, manifold], where manifold is  structure \
returned by  gaDefinePositionVector[ ] command.

Manifold can have few patches, which are  defined inside Piecewise[ ], where \
each entry defines pair of position vector and coordinate range, for which \
the position vector is valid. When none can be applied for safety it is a \
good idea to return $Failed (or False, etc), to be sure at least one patch is \
always applicable. Manifold name (string \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]StandardName\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]) , dimension (string \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Dimension\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]), the number of \
coordinate patches that cover all manifold (string \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Patches\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]) as well as coordinate \
names (string \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]StandardCoordinateNames\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]) and parameters (string \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Parameters\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]) with their range \
assumptions (string \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]ParametersRangeAssumptions\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] are same for entire manifold. On the other hand all \
other data, which are computed inside gaDefineCoordinateSystem[ ], for \
example, metric, reciprocal vectors, etc will be computed for each patch \
separately form the data which are defined by \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Patch1\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Patch2\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], etc. All this very likely  can change during the \
development process.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.887853167217677*^9, 3.88785319207839*^9}, {
  3.887853228327355*^9, 3.887853900343099*^9}, {3.8890834597685547`*^9, 
  3.88908380414785*^9}, {3.88908383793155*^9, 
  3.889083977710791*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"25bd8c82-7ee8-4083-8630-\
77fb67217897"],

Cell["\<\
We will add \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]CS\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] to the end of \
manifold name in the case for coordinate system.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.889084040919001*^9, 3.889084093637645*^9}, 
   3.8890841903676987`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"dd587dc7-80ff-47be-b171-\
7131ca5cd358"]
}, Closed]],

